<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Entitlements for a build signed with a free personal team.

    Deliberately empty. A personal team can sign none of the three the lab build asks for —
    HotspotConfiguration, wifi-info, aps-environment — and an entitlement a team cannot
    grant is a signing failure, not a runtime one, so they are absent rather than requested.

    What that costs, precisely: the app cannot join the experiment AP itself
    (LabInstrument aborts an emit session that declares an accessPoint), and cannot read
    back the SSID it is on, so the session sidecar records an empty ssid. Join the AP by
    hand in Settings and leave accessPoint unset and the rest of the instrument is intact —
    background residency, beacon witnessing, IP_BOUND_IF pinning, the paced emitter and the
    clock exchange need no entitlement at all.

    A session that has to prove which radio it was on needs the lab build. See Config.xcconfig.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
